Greetings to all the gifted blacksmiths!

We have released a brand new patch with bug fixes and gameplay changes.

What's fixed: 
[list]
[*] Bug with incorrect prioritization of orders in the order feed;
[*] Bug that could stop players from receiving a prize for winning a fair;
[*] Incorrect caption in the opt-out option in the second Witches' order;
[*] Graphical bugs in the worker selection menu during events that workers can participate in;
[*] Bug that caused the workbench to need to be replace when Sir Philip arrived, even though it was already placed;
[*] Bug that caused a roof purchased for the first floor to disappear when building a second floor above it;
[*] Bug that caused the construction interface to not disappear after the narrator's line about opening wood orders;
[*] Bug that caused soldiers' lines to double on day 50;
[*] Bug causing the interface to disappear on day 52 when Duke de La Court arrives;
[*] Bug with incorrect animation of Duke de La Court in the wreath;
[*] Bug with flickering plague fog;
[*] Bug with tooltip window flickering on fairs in the tool interface;
[*] Bug with incorrect display of aristocrat phrases during plague;
[*] Bug with incorrect display of reputation hint for mercenaries;
[*] Bug with loading plates with food in the air in some cases;
[*] Bug with incorrect display of modifier textures and the blacksmith's portrait after loading the game in some cases;
[*] Bug with some customers getting stuck after loading the game when they leave the queue;
[*] Incorrect display of pictures in Olivia's second order in the third chapter of the story;
[*] A minor graphical bug with coin accrual at the fair;
[*] Bug with instantaneous loss of character energy after sleeping;
[*] Graphical bug with plague fog disappearing in the background;
[*] Graphics bug with background elements “drifting” after reloading;
[*] Bug with the final illustration in the second fair not displaying correctly in some cases;
[*] Bug with the headman getting stuck on day 33 of the campaign if his story order is not fulfilled;
[*] Bug with the Bandit customer getting stuck on day 52 of the campaign;
[*] System text display in the option to refuse to the bandit on day 52 of the campaign;
[*] Displaying system text in the Order journal when accepting a Bandits' order on day 52 of the campaign;
[*] Bug with bookworm customers getting stuck periodically during the plague;
[*] Typos in the Russian language version of the game;
[*] Graphics bug with blurred portraits of Bandit's aristocrats;
[*] Bug with the incorrect display of the final art on the second fair in some cases;
[*] Bug with the builder missing during construction in some cases after reloading;
[*] Bug with the arrow from the tutorial not disappearing if the player ignores the tutorial;
[*] The incorrect line of Arthur's refusal to order during "The Wine Festival" modifier.
[/list]

What's New:
[list]
[*] Removed the inscription about the effect of the order on relations with factions at fairs;
[*] Wooden orders are now available after setting up a workbench instead of a sawmill.
[*] Now, only customers who are already in the queue are angry at an order completed for a hostile faction. Customers taking their place in the queue no longer react to such an order and do not leave.
[*] Added a new sprite for the stall improvement button if improvement is forbidden.
[*] Blacksmith skills in the interface are now sorted not by skill base level but by base level and equipment bonus. 
[*] Removed the screen darkening around the edges when pausing during dialog.
[/list]
Also, we've added [b]new achievements![/b] Let's see if you can get them all.

Thanks to everyone for the detailed reports and feedback on the game! 


Regards,
Anvil Saga Team

Greetings to all the gifted blacksmiths!

We have released a new patch for Anvil Saga, which contains a variety of fixes and tweaks.

Thank you very much to the community for your feedback and bug reports. 

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40267025/f892e7211362ac4b1a6924eda6efbf8447b8d59d.png[/img]
[olist]
[*] Bug with the camera flying out of frame after scene reloading;
[*] Displaying Arthur instead of other characters after scene reloading;
[*] Characters getting stuck or skipping their dialog when two different characters arrive at the same time;
[*] Masked Bandit aristocrats getting stuck during the plague after completing an order;
[*] Disappearing interface after refusing Bandits on day 50;
[*] No quest after accepting the monk's order on day 7 when using old saves;
[*] Bug with the idle-state of a character working in the mine after reloading;
[*] Actor Vlad getting stuck on the third fair;
[*] Lack of ending for the third fair in some elections;
[*] Lack of art with Baron in the final of the third fair;
[*] Bug that caused the witches' debuff, "Sabbath", does not work;
[*] Bug with "jumping" of the background due to edge scrolling if the game was in a minimized state;
[*] Incorrect display of the number of logs in the interface;
[*] Animations of Monty walking with a plate in his hands while wearing a miner's costume;
[*] Duplication of Louis Surcouf on days 11 and 17 after reloading;
[*] Incorrect display of buffs and debuffs after faction locking;
[*] Appearance of the “Hide the Witch” event at the fair if the event did not occur in the main game;
[*] A cooking furnace collider, which made it impossible to install furniture on floors above or below;
[*] A bug in furniture setup mode that made it possible to place a piece of furniture in front of a door;
[*] The game freezing with the arrival of the dwarves after a restart;
[*] Inability to place some furniture items above the stairs;
[*] Workbench, wood carving machine, and woodworking machine freezing after reloading;
[*] Lack of bonuses from woodcarving tools. (IMPORTANT: this fix will only work in new games – old save files will remain as is);
[*] The "The Greatest Diplomat" achievement being unavailable;
[*] Bug that caused the second order of monks to not give reputation points with the Church when sending two apprentices;
[*] Bug in events with worker selection, that made it possible to send more apprentices than needed, e.g., 2 instead of 1, if the player first chose the option with two and then with one;
[*] Edge scrolling no longer works when the store, hiring menu, and journal are open;
[*] A bug that caused "-2:" instead of "-1" to be displayed when denying Bandit Knights.
[/olist]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40267025/65780eb172ec64ad51b6a1311bb32047b9b2cd9b.png[/img]

Gameplay changes based on feedback:
[list]
[*] Rewritten the order acceptance description in the second witch's order for clarity;
[*] Antonio's store is now always open, even if the rest of the store's functionality is locked;
[*] When sawing a log into planks, workers now take a new log themselves after the old one runs out;
[*] Free equipment from the main game is transferred to fairs, not just the equipment of Arthur and his apprentice;
[*] Added information to the election window for complex orders and side quests that these are optional quests;
[*] Added a hint about the appearance of a separate plaque after opening wooden orders;
[*] Added an indicator for idle blacksmiths;
[*] Added animation of Jean-Jacques working at the third fair;
[*] Added explanations for changing faction relationships when accepting an order and refusing to fulfill an order;
[*] Fixed some of Monty's animations. 
[/list]

Please update the game to try all of these new fixes and changes. If you haven't already, don't forget to join our [url=https://discord.gg/pF2wDA3QrS]Discord[/url], where you can chat with developers and other players.

Regards,
Anvil Saga Team

Greetings to all the gifted blacksmiths!

Thank you to everyone who supports our team by submitting bug reports for Anvil Saga. It helps us to fix things quickly and create the perfect blacksmithing game for you.

After reading the feedback, we realized that the game is very difficult for some people; we have decided to add an easy mode. The gold reward for items and bulk orders is increased by 150%. Bulk orders also provide a 175% boost to reputation, and regular orders grant 2 prestige points. Food in easy mode heals workers to half of their maximum health. Also, the food spoils 1.5 times slower in both modes.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40267025/83f445d3c325be877af105eb5d64e7e0b33eca3d.png[/img]

The following bugs have been fixed: 
[list]
[*] Displaying the incorrect lines for Doan if the player made a frying pan for her;
[*] A bug with the timer before the fair;
[*] Bug where the builder would not arrive to build a room;
[*] Interface blinking on 4K monitors;
[*] Locking buttons on the keyboard after selling a bookcase;
[*] Appearance of empty event windows;
[*] Northener and Finley become stuck during the third fair;
[*] Bug causing an item to still be purchased for a complex order after a customer refused the order and left;
[*] A bug causing progress to reset to zero on day 20;
[*] Bug causing England's order to remain in the order feed in Chapter 3 when accepting a Bandit's order;
[*] Bug causing mixed orders at the fair to bring 0 points;
[*] Bug that caused plank-paid orders to show up as food-paid orders in the order feed;
[*] Ability to hire an extra worker while the current worker was on a task outside the forge;
[*] Displaying a bed instead of a French merchant's order;
[*] Disappearance of the first monk order from the order feed;
[*] Bug causing Vlad's wife to arrive on day 55 after successfully completing all quests on day 53;
[*] Bug with the size of the log rack collider;
[*] Incorrect tooltips in the tutorial;
[*] Bug that caused the religious holidays modifier to start in seasons other than summer;
[*] Bug that caused the stall at the second fair to depend on the results of the preparation for the first fair;
[*] A bug that caused the transition between the two far rooms on the lower level of the mine to not be displayed;
[*] Characters get stuck on the way to the sawmill if it is below ground level.
[*] Bug that caused customers with carving orders to come only in the absence of any modifiers;
[*] Appearance of a black screen instead of a list of completed orders in the Order journal;
[*] Disappearance of the interface in the tutorial after a Baron's order;
[*] Out-of-bounds text in Antonio's first order;
[*] Bug sometimes causing the courier to not bring tools after purchase;
[*] A bug causing a sleep animation on the bed even if the blacksmith is currently awake;
[*] A bug causing a bandit stealing furniture to get stuck after reloading;
[*] Bug that caused the spawn frequency of customers for different modifiers to not be saved;
[*] Bug, because of which, after the completion of Olivia's order in the Order journal entered a record that the order had failed;
[*] Bug with the roof displaying when double-clicking on the design menu;
[*] Fixed several bugs in the Chinese localization. 
[/list]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40267025/7af954fdde672f0d1819a699df0e17777fba6472.png[/img]

In addition, we have added:
[list]
[*] [b]Korean language; [/b]
[*] Ability to refuse Antonio's bulk order on the select tab;
[*] Camera speed settings and edge scrolling, plus the ability to disable them;
[*] Lines about the bells so that players do not assume that blacksmiths not falling asleep during this debuff is a bug. 
[*] Indicators displaying the level when blacksmiths start to require sleep and food;
[*] A display of the current reputation level with the faction in story choices;
[*] A button to open the pause menu;
[*] Dialogues with the bandit stealing furniture when he first arrives; 
[*] Narrator phrases explaining faction mechanics;
[*] Tooltip for orders requiring books.
[/list]
And, finally, we changed the inscription on the fairs. Instead of "Save and Exit" it now says "Exit" to avoid the misconception that you can save at fairs. 

We hope that, despite all of the flaws, you are enjoying Anvil Saga. Thanks again for your help with bugs, support on the release, and feedback on the game.

Regards,
Anvil Saga Team
